div.p:
(1) While we do not have absolute proof, the results of USG investigations support the conclusion that some chemical agent
                    or combination of agents has been used in Laos as part of the Lao Government’s
                    effort to bring the H’mong Hill tribes under its control;

—Démarches by France, UK, FRG, and possibly other interested countries,
                    similar to those already made by the US to the
                    governments of Laos, Vietnam, and the Soviet Union regarding use of CW in Southeast Asia;

A. The US–USSR
                    bilateral negotiations on a CW ban (guidance
                        para 5);
